<title>USA: Key U.S. senator backs CNN bid to open Cuba bureau.</title>
<headline>Key U.S. senator backs CNN bid to open Cuba bureau.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Senate Foreign Relations Committee chairman Jesse Helms said on Thursday he had endorsed CNN's request for a license to open a news bureau in Havana, Cuba.</p>
<p>Cuba said last year it would allow CNN, a division of Time Warner Inc., to establish an office in the Cuban capital, where other non-American foreign news organisations have long been active.</p>
<p>Helms, a sponsor of a law that toughened the embargo against Cuba last year, said that granting a license to Cable News Network would not violate the law &quot;so long as Castro gets nothing in return.&quot;</p>
</text>
